REST is an approach for communication between applications using HTTP.
REST endpoints are specific URL that exposes some functionality.
An endpoint is usually defined by Method type + path(GET /products)

REST Endpoint in Spring

In Spring MVC:

HTTP Request
     ↓
DispatcherServlet
     ↓
Controller
     ↓
Controller Method
     ↓
HTTP Response

A REST endpoint is essentially:

"A controller method mapped to an HTTP method and path."

Traditional :
------------ 
Request
   ↓
Controller
   ↓
View name
   ↓
View Resolver
   ↓
HTML
   ↓
Response
-----------

REST: 
-------
Request
   ↓
Controller
   ↓
Data/Object
   ↓
HTTP Response
------------

Key difference : REST endpoints returns data directly instead of rendering view. The view resolver component isn't involved.

@Controller
    ↓
Usually returns a view

@RestController
    ↓
Returns data directly in HTTP response

Takeaway: 
------------------------------------
REST
 ↓
Application-to-application communication over HTTP
 ↓
Endpoint = HTTP method + path + controller action
 ↓
Spring MVC handles the request
 ↓
Controller returns data
 ↓
No View Resolver
 ↓
Data is sent directly in HTTP response
-------------------------------------

Main advantage: Simple application-to-application communication.

Main concern: The network can fail, requests can time out, data can be large, and servers can become overloaded.
